 ## 2026-07-21
 
+### 0535 — Host VPN production start errors are normalized at both Apple seams (TASK-260715-1rsqrh)
+- FIX: Both iOS and macOS `VPNHostSession` adapters now catch synchronous `NETunnelProviderSession.startTunnel(options:)` errors and translate them through the existing `VPNPreferencePlatformError` model before crossing into `VPNSessionController`. Public `NEVPNError.configurationInvalid`, `.configurationDisabled`, and `.connectionFailed` retain their stable results; every other `NSError` retains its original domain and integer code.
+- INTEGRATION: A freshly loaded exact-owned but disabled manager correctly failed inside `OwnedVPNManagerRepository`, but the controller initially leaked the repository error type. The start preflight now normalizes that one repository result to `VPNSessionControllerError.configurationDisabled` without invoking the system start API or duplicating ownership logic.
+- COVERAGE: An injectable boundary matrix exercises the three public start errors plus an unknown exact domain/code independently through both Apple adapter modules. The real repository-to-controller disabled path asserts zero system start calls and zero manager mutations.
+- VERIFICATION: Focused normal and Thread Sanitizer runs each pass 58 tests in 2 suites; `make validate-core` passes 276 tests in 25 suites plus build; strict Swift format, diff, and board checks pass; sequential iOS Simulator and universal macOS adapter builds succeed.
+
 ### 0526 — Host VPN controller review requests production error-translation rework (TASK-260715-1rsqrh)
 - REVIEW: Focused controller/repository tests pass 57/57, focused TSan passes 23/23, full core validation passes 275/275, strict Swift format and diff checks pass, board validation passes, and both iOS/macOS adapter builds succeed when run sequentially.
 - REGRESSION: `IOSVPNHostSession.startTunnel` and `MacOSVPNHostSession.startTunnel` forward the public `NETunnelProviderSession.startTunnel(options:)` thrown `NSError` unchanged, while `VPNSessionController.performStart` maps only `VPNPreferencePlatformError` / `VPNPlatformError` and otherwise erases the real domain/code to reflected type plus code 0. The unit test injects a pre-normalized fake error, so the production adapter path is untested and cannot satisfy the accepted exact synchronous `NEVPNError` mapping.
